ocd_first_lap patch 0001: fast rear-axle speed getter for the engine powertrain
================================================================================
Approved by Ibrahim: RL-SetupOptimization-Agent docs/DECISIONS.md #8 (2026-10-25).
Applies to: ocd_first_lap working tree at commit 2147dcd PLUS Ibrahim's uncommitted Stage 6
work (the binding.cpp context includes his set_external() hunk). Apply from the
ocd_first_lap root with `git apply` or `patch -p1`, then ./scripts/build.sh.

Why: in engine mode OCDBackend._sync_powertrain runs every 2 ms physics step and read the
rear-axle speed through car.signals([...]), which makes OCD's LoggerComposer rebuild its whole
~220-signal map per call (~18 us, ~1/3 of env step time).

What: Car.rear_axle_omega() in src/binding.cpp returns the drivetrain state element
omega_rear_axle_radps directly. The logged signal 'drivetrain/x_vec/omega_rear_axle_radps'
is a ReferenceLogger pointer to that same double (eqns_.x_vec_), so the value is identical by
construction. VehicleModel keeps drivetrain_model_ protected with no getter, so it is reached
via a member pointer formed in a derived helper struct (standard C++; vendor OCD unchanged,
QA gate's pin+patches check unaffected). signals() and get_telemetry() are unchanged.
_sync_powertrain uses the new getter. A unit test checks getter == signal exactly over 300
engine-mode steps (throttle then brake).

Evidence (2026-10-25, M4): engine-mode Shanghai laps (vmax 12 default brakes; vmax 20 with
12 kN m brakes), the env ScriptedPolicy full lap and 5000 random-action env steps give
identical lap.csv / telemetry.csv sha256, identical obs+reward stream sha256 and identical
full-precision lap time and return before and after. qa_gate.sh PASS before and after.
OCDRacingEnv('Shanghai') throughput, median of 3 x 5000 steps:
random 1893 -> 2939 steps/s, ScriptedPolicy 1817 -> 2952 steps/s.

--- a/src/binding.cpp
+++ b/src/binding.cpp
@@ -16,6 +16,14 @@
   tam::ocd::steering_actuator::PT1SteeringActuatorModel,
   tam::ocd::vehicle_dynamics::VehicleDynamicsDoubleTrackModel<
     tam::ocd::tire_models::MF52, tam::ocd::aerodynamics::RideHeightAerodynamicsModel>>;
+// VehicleModel keeps its drivetrain model protected (in this OCD base class) and has no getter
+// for it. A member pointer formed inside a derived helper reads it without a vendor change.
+using Drivetrain = tam::ocd::drivetrain::DrivetrainModel_RWD_LSD;
+struct DrivetrainAccess : auxiliary::conditional_compilation::DtHelperVehicleModel<
+  Drivetrain, tam::ocd::steering_actuator::PT1SteeringActuatorModel,
+  Drivetrain::AuxiliaryInputType> {
+  static Drivetrain const & of(Veh const & v) { return v.*&DrivetrainAccess::drivetrain_model_; }
+};
 struct Car {
   Veh v;
   void set_parameters(py::dict values) {
@@ -56,6 +64,13 @@
     }
     return out;
   }
+  // Rear-axle speed [rad/s]: the same double as signal 'drivetrain/x_vec/omega_rear_axle_radps'
+  // (that log entry points at this state element). The engine powertrain reads it every 2 ms
+  // step; signals() rebuilds the whole ~220-signal log map per call (~18 us), this does not.
+  double rear_axle_omega() const {
+    return DrivetrainAccess::of(v).get_x_vec()[
+      tam::ocd::drivetrain::rwd_lsd::States::omega_rear_axle_radps];
+  }
   // Road height under each wheel [FL, FR, RL, RR] (z up, needs patches/0002) and a force and
